{"id":"word:hebrew:H1964","type":"word","title":"הֵיכָל","subtitle":"H1964 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a large public building, such as a palace or temple","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to הֵיכָל (H1964) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 80 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"הֵיכָל (hêykâl) means a large public building, such as a palace or temple First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 6 3."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"הֵיכָל","transliteration":"hêykâl","pronunciation":"hay-kawl'","strong":"H1964","lemmaId":"hebrew:H1964","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["הֵיכַ֣ל","בְּ/הֵיכַ֣ל","הֵיכַ֤ל","הֵיכַ֥ל","הַ/הֵיכָ֖ל"],"morphs":[["HNcmsc",21],["HTd/Ncmsa",15],["HR/Ncmsc",14],["HRd/Ncmsa",6],["HR/Ncmsc/Sp3ms",4],["HNcmsa",3],["HNcmsc/Sp3ms",3],["HC/Td/Ncmsa",2],["HR/Ncmpc",2],["HNcmsc/Sp2ms",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"a large public building, such as a palace or temple","usage":"palace, temple.","full":"H1964. hekal הֵיכָל noun masculine Nahum 2:7 (on Isa 44:28 compare Che Di) palace, temple (see also Late Hebrew id. temple , Aramaic הֵיכְלָא הֵיכָלָא, , , palace, temple , Palmyrene הכלא temple Vog 16 ; compare Arabic (probably Aramaic loan-word according to Frä 274 ), Ethiopic temple ; Assyrian ekallu , palace, temple ; — probably loan-word from Akkadian e-gal , great house , compare Schr HI 148 COT 2Kin 20:18 Hpt E-vowel 11 f. Lehmann Šamaššumukîn 126 , and on usage Dl 338 ; &gt; from יכל ( וכל ) = כול contain Ew § 162 b Thes Add 84 ; compare Ol § 191 b Hoffm AGG xxxvi. Mai 1889:25 Dl w ; from an original יכל Lag BN 121 , but compare Hom ZMG 1890.547 ) absolute ׳ה Amos 8:3 27t. ( ׳הַה 1Kin 6:17 +); construct הֵיכַל Micah 1:2 35t.; suffix הֵיכָלָ֑ךָ Psa 48:10 2 t.; הֵיכָלוֺ Jer 50:28 7 t.; plural הֵיכָלוֺת Hosea 8:14 ; construct הֵיכְלֵי Isa 13:22 2 t.; suffix הֵיכְלֵיכֶם Joel 4:5; &#8212; never in Hexateuch, rarely in Samuel & pre-exile prophets; especially frequently in Ki Ezekiel & late prophets, also Chronicles; occasionally in Psalms; &#8212; 1 rather seld . (royal) palace (so almost always in Assyrian); of Ahab 1Kin 21:1 , of king of Babylon 2Kin 20:18 = Isa 38:17 ; 2Chr 36:7 , compare Dan 1:4 , and plural עֹנֶג הֵיכְלֵי Isa 13:22 luxurious palaces ; at Nineveh ׳וְהַה נָמוֺג Nahum 2:7 ; not clearly defined are מֶלֶךְ הֵיכַל Psa 45:16 and שֵׁן הֵיכְלֵי 45:9 ; הֵיכָלוֺת Hosea 8:14 (in Northern Israel); see also הַהוּא בַּיּוֺם הֵיכָל שִׁירוֺת וְהֵילִילוּ Amos 8:3 and palace-songs shall be howlings in that day ; compare also (probably) of Phoenician palaces Joel 4:5; quite General מֶלֶךְ הֵיכְלֵי , Prov 30:28 , & הֵיכָל תַּבְנִית Psa 144:12 (simile of well-proportioned daughters); — usual term for royal palace in Hebrew is הַמֶּלֶךְ בֵּית , see בית . 2 of palace of God considered as king , = house of God or of ׳י , temple (compare ׳הַה Isa 6:1 e. below where prophet sees עַלכִּֿסֵּא ישֵׁב אדני ): a. of early, pre-Solomonic house at Shiloh י ׳הֵיכַל 1Sam 1:9 ; 3:3 (= י ׳בֵּית 1:7 ; 3:15 ; מוֺעֵד אֹהֶל מֶּתַח 2:22 omitted by ᵐ5 We Klo Dr) with doors ( דלתות , 3:15 ) & a doorpost ( מזוזה 1:9 ) (compare 2Sam 22:7 = Psa 18:7 e below). b. of Solomon's temple : specifically the hall or nave of the temple (the holy place, distinguished from the דְּבִּיר the inner sanctuary, the Holy of Holies, and with this included in the more General term י ׳בֵּית or הַבַּיִת , 1Kin 6:1-2 ,+ often) 6:17 (compare 6:19 ; 6:20 & 6:2 ) also 6:5 ; 6:33 ; 7:50 2Chr 4:22 ; further 4:7-8 , Ezek 8:16 (twice in verse) הַבַּיִת הֵיכַל עַלמְּֿנֵי הָאוּלָם 1Kin 6:3 ; הַהֵיכָל אֻלָם 7:21 || הַהֵיכָל עַלמְּֿנֵי 2Chr 3:17 ; י ׳הֵיכַל 2Kin 18:16 ; also in wide sense (apparently = י ׳בֵּית ), י ׳הֵיכַל 23:4 ; 24:13 (|| י ׳בֵּית ), Jer 7:4 (3 t. in verse) (|| י ׳בֵּית 7:2 ), 24:1 see also הֵיכָלוֺ נִקְמַת 50:28 ; 51:11 (both || י ׳נִקְמַת ); 2Chr 26:16 ; 27:2 , compare 29:16 (|| י בֵית ׳מְּנִ֫ימָה ; opposed to ב ׳חֲצַר ׳י ), in all three י ׳הֵיכַל . c. hall or nave of Ezekiel's temple, the holy place (see above) (included in הַבַּיִת , the General term embracing the whole group of buildings) Ezek 41:1 , 4 , 15 , 21 , 23 , 25 (compare 41:20 ) 42:8 . d. general designation of 2 nd temple , הַהֵיכָל Zech 8:9 (|| י ׳בֵּית צְבָאוֺת ); oftener י ׳הֵיכַל Hag 2:15 , 18 ; Zech 6:12-13 , 14 , 15 ; Ezra 3:6 , 10 , הֵיכָלוֺ Mal 3:1 ; Psa 27:4 ; יִשְׂרָאֵל אֱלֹהֵי ליהוה הֵיכָל בּוֺנִים Ezra 4:1 ; (הַ)הֵיכָל Neh 6:10 (twice in verse) (|| הָאֱלֹהִים בֵּית ), 6:11 ; Isa 44:28 , compare also 66:6 . &#8212; הֵיכָל occurs occasionally in Psalms, without conclusive evidence, in all cases, to what temple reference is had; apparently distinguished from י ׳בֵּית (as below b ) Psa 5:8 ( קָדְשְׁךָ הֵיכַל ; see בֵּיתֶ֑ךָ 5:7 ); perhaps also 68:30 (distinguished from Holy of Holies by De Che; yet verse obscure); but no distinction evident 79:1 ; 138:2 ; Jonah 2:5 ; 2:8 (all קָדְשְׁךָ הֵיכַל ); compare הֵיכָל֑ךָ קְדשׁ Psa 65:5 (|| בֵּיתֶ֑ךָ ); as containing the worshipping assembly 48:10 . e. of the heavenly temple where ׳י sits enthroned Isa 6:1 ; his abode in the heavens 2Sam 22:7 = Psa 18:7 ; 11:4 (|| שָׁמַיִם ; compare קָדְשׁוֺ זְבֻל Isa 63:15 , || id. ), 29:9 ; קָדְשׁוֺ מֵהֵיכַל אֲדֹנָי Micah 1:2 , compare Hab 2:20 קָדְשׁוֺ בְּהֵיכַל ויהוה .","rootNote":"probably from 3201 (in the sense of capacity );","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 6 3","keyReferences":["1Kgs 6 3","1Kgs 6 5","1Kgs 6 17","1Kgs 6 33","1Kgs 7 21","1Kgs 7 50","1Kgs 21 1","1Sam 1 9"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":80,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 6 3","book":"1Kgs","chapter":6,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הֵיכַ֣ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 6 5","book":"1Kgs","chapter":6,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לַֽ/הֵיכָ֖ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HRd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Kg